<p>President Theodore Roosevelt embarked on a nine-and-a-half-week journey across the North American continent in April 1903. The Pennsylvania Railroad Company provided a special six-car train, decorated and equipped for a 14,000-mile cross-country journey. Mandan was one of five stops included in North Dakota. Roosevelt wanted to personally talk to people and give an account of his previous term in office. It was also an opportunity for him to visit Yellowstone National Park accompanied by the famous naturalist John Burroughs.</p>

