<p>TR Speech at Mandan Leaving Washington, D.C., on April 1, 1903, he arrived in North Dakota six days later. Fargo was his first and longest stop in the state. Arriving early in the morning, he was escorted to the business district where he was greeted by several thousand children. From a stand in front of the Waldorf Hotel, Roosevelt discussed his administration’s Philippine policy. The train subsequently stopped for approximately 30 minutes in Jamestown.</p>

