<p>In Bismarck,, President Roosevelt shuttled by carriage to the Capitol where he repeated much of his speech from Fargo, was greeted by chiefs and other members of area Native American tribes and was treated to a barbecue of ox and apple cider. Carriage ride in Bismarck to Capitol Indian Chiefs in Attendance</p>

<p>After the three-hour stop, TR returned to his train and they moved on to Mandan. He spoke from a stand erected on the north side of the depot especially for the occasion. After completing his speech, he returned to his railcar and was joined by friend and Badlands frontier guide Joe Ferris and his brother and former Elkhorn Ranch foreman Sylvane Ferris. Perfecto Fernández also known as Georgie Baye, another ranch hand acquaintance, was also welcomed aboard for the ride to Medora. (Roosevelt orchestrated his naturalization to a U.S. citizen when TR was president.)</p>

